.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt SEND_SIGNAL 2
.Os Project9
.Sh NAME
.Nm send_signal
.Nd signal a process or process group
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In types.h
.In user.h
.In signal.h
.Ft int
.Fn send_signal "int pid" "int sig"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A positive
.Fa pid
selects one process, zero selects the caller's group and a value less
than -1 selects the group whose ID is its absolute value.
The value -1 selects eligible processes other than the caller.
Signal 0 checks existence and permission.
Root and processes with the same UID can send signals.
CONT can also be sent within the same login session.
Init is protected from delivery.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The function returns 0 if it finds an eligible process, or -1 on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kill 1 ,
.Xr waitpid 2
